  "text": "אוהב\n\nTo find the coordinates of vertex \\( A \\), we need to use the given information about the midpoints \\( M \\) and \\( N \\).\n\nFirst, let's use the midpoint formula. The midpoint of a line segment with endpoints \\((x_1, y_1, z_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2, z_2)\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \\frac{y_1 + y_2}{2}, \\frac{z_1 + z_2}{2} \\right)\n\\]\n\nFor midpoint \\( M(3, -1, 5) \\) of \\(\\overline{AG}\\), we have:\n\\[\nM = \\left( \\frac{a + (a+3)}{2}, \\frac{b + (b+4)}{2}, \\frac{c + (c+2)}{2} \\right)\n\\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[\nM = \\left( \\frac{2a+3}{2}, \\frac{2b+4}{2}, \\frac{2c+2}{2} \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\nM = \\left( a + \\frac{3}{2}, b + 2, c + 1 \\right)\n\\]\nSince \\( M(3, -1, 5) \\), we can set up the following equations:\n\\[\na + \\frac{3}{2} = 3\n\\]\n\\[\nb + 2 = -1\n\\]\n\\[\nc + 1 = 5\n\\]\nSolving these equations, we get:\n\\[\na = 3 - \\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{6}{2} - \\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -1 - 2 = -3\n\\]\n\\[\nc = 5 - 1 = 4\n\\]\n\nNext, for midpoint \\( N(-1, 1, -1) \\) of \\(\\overline{FH}\\), we have:\n\\[\nN = \\left( \\frac{a + (-1)}{2}, \\frac{b + (b+4)}{2}, \\frac{c + (-1)}{2} \\right)\n\\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[\nN = \\left( \\frac{a - 1}{2}, \\frac{2b + 4}{2}, \\frac{c - 1}{2} \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\nN = \\left( \\frac{a - 1}{2}, b + 2, \\frac{c - 1}{2} \\right)\n\\]\nSince \\( N(-1, 1, -1) \\), we can set up the following equations:\n\\[\n\\frac{a - 1}{2} = -1\n\\]\n\\[\nb + 2 = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{c - 1}{2} = -1\n\\]\nSolving these equations, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{a - 1}{2} = -1 \\implies a - 1 = -2 \\implies a = -1\n\\]\n\\[\nb + 2 = 1 \\implies b = -1\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{c - 1}{2} = -1 \\implies c - 1 = -2 \\implies c = -1\n\\]\n\nWe see that there is a contradiction in the values of \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\) from the two midpoints. This suggests that there might be an error in the problem statement or the interpretation of the vertices. However, based on the given information and the midpoint formulas, the coordinates of vertex \\( A \\) are:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left( \\frac{3}{2}, -3, 4 \\right)}\n\\]",
